6. Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

data/external/ja_tts_g2p_bench_v1.jsonl and eval_results/table_a3_ja_reading/
contain items of ja-tts-g2p-bench (kawajiri-tellernovel/ja-tts-g2p-bench,
CC BY-SA 4.0), redistributed under that license; see data/external/README.md.

The voice-cloning prompts (LibriTTS, JSUT, the Databaker Chinese Standard
Mandarin Speech Corpus, FLEURS) are not redistributed, except the one JSUT
recording on the sample page (docs/audio/prompt/, under the JSUT terms quoted in
docs/LICENSE_AUDIO.md). scripts/prepare_voice_prompts.py rebuilds the prompts
from the original corpora. No synthesized audio is redistributed apart from the
listening-test clips of the sample page (docs/); the generated waveforms clone a
prompt speaker's voice, so the repository releases the item lists, the scoring
code, and the per-sample scores instead.
